WEBVTT

00:00:00.230 --> 00:00:02.670
AssentTag starts with a group photo.

00:00:02.670 --> 00:00:07.242
OpenCV finds faces and Dlib compares
them with enrolled identities.

00:00:07.598 --> 00:00:09.789
A face match still needs permission.

00:00:09.789 --> 00:00:13.266
The Django app blurs the face until it
has consent.

00:00:13.266 --> 00:00:14.884
MySQL stores the records.

00:00:15.265 --> 00:00:18.306
Next, evaluate missed faces and masking
failures

00:00:18.306 --> 00:00:21.255
on a representative, consented dataset.

00:00:21.938 --> 00:00:24.918
On a palm leaf, faint writing can
resemble grain.

00:00:24.918 --> 00:00:28.704
EpigraphiX-AI uses adaptive thresholds
to separate the two.

00:00:29.057 --> 00:00:32.590
Python and OpenCV isolate connected
marks as glyphs.

00:00:32.590 --> 00:00:36.549
A Malayalam lexicon helps review likely
character sequences.

00:00:36.890 --> 00:00:39.566
Next, connect a trained recognition
model

00:00:39.566 --> 00:00:43.283
and measure character and word errors
on unseen manuscripts.

00:00:43.938 --> 00:00:47.619
AegisForge-X makes a security finding
traceable to the source.

00:00:47.973 --> 00:00:50.960
Python masks comments while preserving
positions.

00:00:50.960 --> 00:00:53.393
Language rules flag potential issues,

00:00:53.393 --> 00:00:57.145
and hashes link evidence to the
reviewed input for human inspection.

00:00:57.515 --> 00:01:00.258
Next, use labeled examples to measure
false alarms

00:01:00.258 --> 00:01:03.306
and missed cases for each language and
rule.

00:01:03.980 --> 00:01:07.471
Deciphera is a browser simulator for
Bitcoin transfers.

00:01:07.848 --> 00:01:10.421
JavaScript models an off-chain
transaction,

00:01:10.421 --> 00:01:13.356
then turns the same event into three
explanations:

00:01:13.356 --> 00:01:16.960
one for a client, one for an auditor,
and one for a technical reader.

00:01:17.307 --> 00:01:19.933
Next, add tests that compare each
narrative

00:01:19.933 --> 00:01:22.712
with an explicitly defined transaction
state.

00:01:23.397 --> 00:01:24.905
QuietNote tackles a race:

00:01:24.905 --> 00:01:27.564
two readers opening a one-time link
together.

00:01:27.932 --> 00:01:30.448
Next.js and Hono handle the request.

00:01:30.448 --> 00:01:34.623
One conditional PostgreSQL update lets
a single reader claim the note.

00:01:34.623 --> 00:01:37.741
Owners can also set expiry or revoke
access.

00:01:38.098 --> 00:01:42.668
Next, add retention controls and test
the counters under heavier traffic.

